In article <2271@wheaton.UUCP> kroth@wheaton.UUCP (Ken Roth) writes:
>In article <1990Sep26.055043.1105@midway.uchicago.edu> zama@ellis.uchicago.edu (iftikhar uz zaman) writes:
>>So here's the question: what does "No regen" mean next to Excalibur?
>>That wielding this weapon will inhibit your regeneration???

Obviously, this is a result of somebody mis-reading the artifact code.  There
is no "no regen" for Excalibur or any other weapon.  Instead, somebody is
mistaking SPFX_NOGEN, which simply means that the particular weapon is one
granted by a deity.  It doesn't have anything to do with regeneration of you
or any other creature.

>Also to be honest, the whole Special weapon thing confuses me, as I know about
>three things about C.

Ok.  Here's the deal:  For the damage listed under the weapons section, each
weapon will do between 1 and x points of damage with a successful hit, where
x is taken from the L or S column, depending on what the size of the monster
just hit is.  Certain weapons also get other bonuses (for instance, a broad
sword always gets +1 damage), and you also get additional damage on a point
for point basis for the bonus of the weapon.  

Artifacts (named weapons) can do additional damage on top of that.  The 
regular damage for an artifact is computed, depending on the weapon type,
and then an additional 1 to x damage is added depending on the damage bonus
listed under the appropriate column for the artifact.  Finally, (and I'm not
totally sure on this point) I believe that if a 0 is listed under the damage
modifier for the artifact, it doubles the regular damage instead of adding 
a bonus of its own.

Is this understandable?

